# Pin the public npm registry for this package.
#
# Without this, npm inherits the registry from the user's global ~/.npmrc, and any
# `npm install` rewrites every `resolved` URL in package-lock.json to point at that
# registry. A lockfile is a published artifact: those URLs would ship to consumers,
# who cannot reach a private mirror — and, for anyone running behind one, would leak
# its hostname into a public repository.
#
# Pinning here keeps the lockfile reproducible and host-neutral regardless of the
# developer's environment. To build through a local mirror anyway, override it for
# the command only, without touching the lockfile:
#
#   npm_config_registry=https://your-mirror.example/ npm ci
#
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
